WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.176
A trader can be right about the final price and still be liquidated along the way.

00:00:04.176 --> 00:00:11.049
Tend gives BTC and ETH traders a different contract: a fixed premium, capped upside, and no liquidation.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:13.683
This is the actual app running on Monad testnet.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.793
Switch from Bitcoin to Ethereum and the market chart updates with real Coinbase prices.

00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:22.683
The data path checks freshness and rejects missing or malformed prices.

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:25.884
A data failure stops quoting instead of inventing a number.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.814
Choose up or down, an expiry schedule, and the premium you are willing to lose.

00:00:30.814 --> 00:00:35.921
The exact expiry is shown because a scheduled market is not a new full duration from purchase.

00:00:35.921 --> 00:00:41.169
Twenty-five times means maximum payout divided by premium, not a guaranteed return.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.566
At the fill, the vault locks the position's maximum payout and enforces its risk limits.

00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:51.814
The pool view reads assets, locked collateral, and open obligations directly from Monad.

00:00:51.814 --> 00:00:55.753
Here, the completed rehearsal has settled and its collateral is released.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:01:02.283
This is historical position ten, completed earlier today through the live quote API and a command-line wallet.

00:01:02.283 --> 00:01:05.453
The buyer paid just under one hundred mock USDC.

00:01:05.453 --> 00:01:10.841
The vault escrowed two thousand five hundred mock USDC, and the receipt records the checks.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:15.903
MonadScan shows the successful fill and the exact premium transfer into the vault.

00:01:15.903 --> 00:01:19.329
The rehearsal reconciled the buyer's balance and collateral lock.

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:23.681
This is an actual testnet transaction, not a simulated success screen.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.671
After the real expiry, the position settled successfully with a payout of zero.

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:34.546
The premium was the entire trading loss, excluding network gas, and collateral returned to the pool.

00:01:34.546 --> 00:01:41.338
The demo uses a real Coinbase expiry-minute price through MockPyth, which does not authenticate oracle attestations.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:49.862
September work adds model-based pricing, expiry ladders, indicative marks, and realized trade history to an existing foundation.

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:54.231
Monad supports the EVM contracts and short-lived signed quote flow shown here.

00:01:54.231 --> 00:02:01.869
This remains a testnet demo: mock collateral, mock oracle verification, no early exit, and a keeper scheduling gap.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:05.906
Explore the app and inspect the receipts at monad dot usetend dot xyz.
